// The bird: how far down it is, which wing frame it is on, and how far over it
// has tipped.

// The spacer above the bird. On the ready screen `bob` adds a gentle hover, so
// the same expression serves both the title screen and the flight.
bird_top() {
  int y = (import g)[1] / 100 + bob();
} return string pct(y, 512);

// Three wing frames at ten a second while it flies; the wing locks flat the
// moment the bird is hit, so the death fall reads as a dead weight.
bird_src() {
  int f = (import g)[6] / 6 % 3;
  if ((import g)[0] > 1) { f = 1; }
} return string "/sprites/bird-" + f + ".svg";

// A class rather than an inline angle: idml styles elements through classes and
// dimensions, so the twelve tilt steps live in the stylesheet and id just picks
// one. Twelve steps is about what the original shows.
bird_rot() {
} return string "fb-r" + tilt();
